coverage:
I read all of the LaTeX in build/paper/ (sections 01-10 and appendix A) at referee depth. Things I checked by computation:
(1) Section 6 palette identities. With random numerical matrix models (M_3(C), * = conjugate transpose) I checked that the affine-to-fractional formula agrees up to a central scalar, that a abar - b bbar = -l(theta - thetabar)^2, that z = w R_C, the two commutations [vw, uz] = 1 and [w^{-1}v, z^{-1}u'] = 1, the translation vector b_w, the t/d formula, and B_w(l,s).
(2) By hand, I checked that the double-coset relation gives ZW in C(B)(ZW^{-1})C(BZ^2) with the commutations assigned correctly.
(3) Symbolically, I checked that L_x v(y) reproduces the scalar parameters of y x^{-1} and that ker L_x = k v(x).
(4) Symbolically, I checked that g_s in Lemma rec:field-rotations is affine with multiplier m_s.
(5) Numerically, I checked all Section 8 identities: Sylvester solution, the pair move, P*P = Q + Q*, the three-unitary identity 1 - P Q^{-1} P* = m_b m_z m_e^*, and m_b unitary.
(6) Numerically, I checked the Section 9 factorization identities (z, h = PP'P + ..., h = zz*, h commuting with P and P', and the block formula for h_+ with equal characteristic polynomials). By hand I checked the 2x2 block z, the pole Newton-polygon slopes and the cycle model.
(7) Against ATLAS data, I checked the sporadic table (|F| > k c^4 in every row, smallest margin M11) and the exceptional-group numerics.
I also checked by hand:
- the norm-torus lattice argument, including the m = 4 integral obstruction and the sign-element cocycle;
- the local abelianization filtration;
- the circle-extension splitting and finite-character extraction;
- the char-2 period-group argument and the Frobenius-expansion density proof;
- the odd-char quadric orthogonality (it uses I_j * I_j inside H_j);
- the degree-four multinorm correction (r_0 in J_0^1, d = c_* + r_0 cbar_*);
- the binary-smallness uniformity (local fields of char p are F_q'((T)), so the threshold is intrinsic).
I accepted cited inputs without re-deriving them: CFSG/Feit-Seitz, Prasad-Rapinchuk metaplectic kernel, Demarche-Harari duality, Howe-Moore, RSS inner type A, global Kneser-Tits, Fulman-Guralnick class bounds. I spot-checked the classical-group (PSU/PSp/orthogonal) block arguments in the appendix for plausibility but did not verify every case in detail.
